    "allow_multiple_attempts": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Bug 1\r\n\r\nThe bug I experienced was that when I added a new stop, the notes didn’t match the correct stop. My guess was that one of the arrays wasn’t being updated when adding a stop. AI suggested that the arrays might be out of sync and that all arrays need to be updated together.\r\n\r\nThe correct fix was to add `stopNotesArray.push(notes)` in the `addStop()` function. This happened because only some of the arrays were updated, so the data no longer matched across the route.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Bug 2\r\n\r\nThe bug I experienced was that after removing a stop, the hours didn’t match the correct stop anymore. My guess was that one of the arrays wasn’t removing an item when I clicked remove. AI suggested that the arrays could be getting out of sync and that each array should be updated when removing data.\r\n\r\nThe correct fix was to add `stopHoursArray.pop()` in the `removeStop()` function. This happened because one array still had extra data, so the values were shifted and didn’t line up correctly.\r\n"
  },
